 Unity/URP are not vendored. Package versions are recorded in `Packages/manifest.json` and `Packages/packages-lock.json`.
 
+iOS 27 requires the UIScene lifecycle when building with its SDK. The project retains the licensed 2022.3.62f3 Editor and runtime and applies a project-owned native lifecycle bridge to iOS exports. Its native checks and signed Release build pass; login, character selection, world entry, walking and camera control work on an iPhone 14 Pro Max. This custom integration follows Unity's manual migration guidance; it is not a Unity-supported backport. Broader gameplay and device checks remain pending; see the [iPhone validation record](IOS.md).
+
 ## Open the project
 
 Clone the repository, then add its root folder to Unity Hub as an existing project. Let Unity restore packages and import resources. Open `Assets/Scenes/Game.unity`; Game is the supported build scene. MapTest was removed.
 
+Keep the Unity project, generated `Library/` cache and build outputs outside iCloud-synced folders. Sync conflict copies of generated assemblies can break IL2CPP builds. For the current iPhone validation, `/private/tmp/openfusion-pocket-ios-local` is a disposable staging copy containing clean build inputs; the original source workspace remains authoritative.
+
 Runtime resources are obtained through the launcher and selected server. You do not need to commit or copy a personal launcher cache, account data or game bundles into the source tree.
 
 ## Build an APK
