@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# UIScene backport regression
+
+From any directory, run:
+
+```sh
+/path/to/OpenFusion-Pocket/tests/IOSSceneLifecycleTest/run.sh
+```
+
+The runner finds the local `.tools/dotnet/dotnet` SDK in the project or its parent,
+then uses the installed Unity 2022.3.62f3 iOS module. Override either path when needed:
+
+```sh
+tests/IOSSceneLifecycleTest/run.sh \
+  --dotnet /path/to/.tools/dotnet/dotnet \
+  --ios-module /Applications/Unity/Hub/Editor/2022.3.62f3/PlaybackEngines/iOSSupport \
+  --export /private/tmp/my-existing-ios-export
+```
+
+`DOTNET_EXE` and `UNITY_IOS_MODULE` are also supported. `--export` is optional: it
+runs the same checks against a temporary copy of that export after checking the
+installed template. The supplied export and installed Unity files remain untouched.
+
+The test copies only the needed controller/header, Unity view/view-handler sources,
+plist and Xcode project into a
+temporary directory. It applies the project-owned bridge twice using the installed
+Unity Xcode library, then compares every generated file, including `project.pbxproj`,
+byte for byte. This catches duplicate native source membership on repeated export
+postprocessing. It also checks connected-scene startup, retained-window reconnection,
+unchanged `.62` runtime startup/rendering code, cold-link ordering, all four original
+lifecycle callbacks, scene metadata preservation and rejection of unknown source.
+Live surface scale and view-controller transitions use the attached window scene's
+screen, falling back to the window's screen and then the initial main screen before
+attachment. The fixture preserves Unity's initial unattached-view setup and rejects
+unknown, mixed or duplicated live-scale replacements before any export files change.
+The iOS 27 scene-level orientation callback forwards Unity's live orientation mask
+after preserving landscape startup. The wider resizable-scene plist therefore does
+not replace the runtime's ordinary-phone landscape and inner-hinge rotation policy.
+
+The project has no NuGet package dependencies. Restore sources point to a nonexistent
+local directory and NuGet audit is disabled, so the test does not require NuGet
+network access. No proprietary Unity templates are included in the repository.
+
+This is a source-export regression. It does not launch Unity or Xcode, compile the
+native player, change a license, or establish physical-device runtime behavior.
