@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Platform boundary checks
+
+These standalone checks compile the production `PocketPlatform` and `PocketUpdater` classes against small host substitutes. They check that iOS and desktop cannot request Android releases, download APKs or invoke the Android bridge, that unavailable credential storage fails closed, and that the Android bridge/update checks remain enabled on Android.
+
+With a .NET 8 SDK, run each compilation branch from the project root:
+
+```sh
+dotnet run --project tests/IosPlatformTest/IosPlatformTest.csproj -p:PocketTestTarget=iOS
+dotnet run --project tests/IosPlatformTest/IosPlatformTest.csproj -p:PocketTestTarget=Android
+dotnet run --project tests/IosPlatformTest/IosPlatformTest.csproj -p:PocketTestTarget=Desktop
+```
+
+On macOS with Apple's command line tools, check native credential behavior using an in-memory substitute for the Security framework's storage operations:
+
+```sh
+xcrun clang++ -fobjc-arc -Wall -Wextra -Werror -framework Foundation -framework Security tests/IosPlatformTest/KeychainTest.mm -o /tmp/openfusion-keychain-test
+/tmp/openfusion-keychain-test
+```
+
+The native test checks device-only/unlocked attributes, UTF-8 password roundtrips, updates and scoped deletion. It does not read or modify the host's Keychain. The C# tests do not load the Apple native library.
+
+These are host checks. A Unity iOS export, IL2CPP compilation, Xcode linking and signed iPhone tests are still required, including actual Keychain save/load/forget across app restarts and confirming that iPhone updates show no APK actions.
