@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Runs the production third-person `TouchCameraRig.cs` without Unity:
+
+```sh
+dotnet run --project tests/TouchCameraFollowTest
+```
+
+Numerical perspective projection checks readable body framing across plausible
+avatar heights, camera height relative to the head, and invalid or implausible
+imported bounds. Across 131 avatar heights, the closest zoom must keep the full
+body visible at the default pitch and both pitch limits. Extreme, one-metre and
+nonfinite zoom requests must leave a finite third-person orbit, and clamping
+must remain monotonic and stable under repeated application.
+
+Movement, touch ownership and collision handling are covered separately by
+`Assets/Editor/IOSInputChecks.cs`, which runs against the production Unity code.
+This standalone suite does not confirm device feel or the runtime bounds source.
