+# Initial-world preparation regression
+
+Run `python3 tests/WorldLoadPreparationTest/run.py` from the project, or invoke its
+absolute path from another directory. The runner finds the local `.tools/dotnet`
+SDK in the project or its parent; `DOTNET_EXE` overrides that path. No NuGet network
+access, Unity run, downloaded game resources or phone connection is needed.
+
+The harness extracts the current `LoadWorldAsync` body directly from production
+source. Its only substitution replaces the 250 ms map-wait delay with a virtual
+clock. Controlled fake download/loader dependencies hold shared preparation open,
+then advance its duration to the observed 136,201 ms. The checks verify:
+
+- No map polling or map timeout starts before shared preparation finishes.
+- Both download phases receive progress and preparation uses the downloaded phase.
+- The existing phase shared-file list supplies preparation, rather than map files.
+- Successful already-loaded targets retain the previous unpaused behavior.
+- Download/preparation errors propagate without entering the map wait.
+- A stalled map still receives the full existing 120-second map-build budget.
+
+All generated harness files stay in a temporary directory and are removed afterward.
